++- **A sub-agent's tool calls fire the same PreToolUse hooks, and the input names the sub-agent** (https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks, read 2026-10-02): "When a subagent calls a tool, tool events such as `PreToolUse` and `PostToolUse` fire the same configured hooks as in the main conversation, and the input carries the `agent_id` and `agent_type` common input fields that identify the subagent." `agent_id` is "Present only when the hook fires inside a subagent call". The `panel_blind` hook does not depend on it: its rule (no Read or Grep of one blind verdict while the other is missing) holds for every caller. SubagentStop's input fields and a model field in a sub-agent's transcript are not documented on the hooks or sub-agents pages.
